Backend JavaScript developers spend hundreds of hours integrating Stripe Webhooks, building billing database tables, and managing customer subscriptions.

With `apay-gateway` on NPM, you can protect any Express route with sub-millisecond HTTP 402 micro-billing in 3 lines of code:

```typescript
import express from 'express';
import { apayMiddleware } from 'apay-gateway/express';

const app = express();

// Protect endpoint with $0.005 micro-settlement
app.use('/v1/premium-data', apayMiddleware({ price: '0.005' }));

app.get('/v1/premium-data', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'success', data: 'Protected compute delivered!' });
});
```

⚡ Why developers love `apay-gateway`:
• Zero database roundtrips: Validates EIP-712 signatures in memory in under 3ms
• Automatic RFC HTTP 402 challenge formatting with Base L2 receiver headers
• 100% type-safe with full TypeScript declarations

